Priya (Customer): Hi team, onboarding hit a snag. After pushing the browser devkit to staging we see spike of 429s during page loads. Happens when users open multiple tabs or during CI parallel runs. Renewal check penciled in next week, so we need a quick stabilization plan.
Anya (CS): Ugh. Can you share the example error and where the SDK is running (edge function, serverless, SPA)? Also SDK version?
Priya (Customer): SDK 1.3.0-alpha, running in edge serverless (Vercel). Error: `POST /v1/preflight 429 "rate_limit_exceeded"` in our staging logs. We see many parallel POSTs from the same IP within seconds.
Raj (SRE): Sounds like a preflight + ephemeral token fanout. Two immediate mitigation paths: 1) client fixes (de-dupe/init), 2) temporary account burst. Which do you prefer short-term?
Priya (Customer): Both, if possible. We can patch client faster but a short quota increase would give breathing room for rollout.
Lena (SDK Eng): For client-side de-dupe, implement a singleflight/inflight promise cache instead of per-request token fetch. Example (node/browser shared):
```js
const inflight = new Map();
async function initOnce(){
  if(inflight.has('init')) return inflight.get('init');
  const p = (async()=>{
    // small jitter to avoid sync
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.random()*200));
    const res = await fetch('/v1/preflight', {method:'POST'});
    if(!res.ok) throw new Error('preflight failed');
    return res.json();
  })();
  inflight.set('init', p);
  try { return await p; } finally { inflight.delete('init'); }
}
```
Lena (SDK Eng): Also recommend session-level token leases (cache for 60s) and a local in-memory token-bucket to stop bursts across multiple requests from the same runtime.
Raj (SRE): On our end we can open a temporary burst window on the account and enable a soft preflight queue (convert surges to 202+in-queue for 30s) for onboarding traffic. DM me the account ID + desired hours.
Priya (Customer): Account PRYA-2202. Requesting 24h burst window while we roll the patched devkit across staging->prod.
Anya (CS): Got it — filing the quota request now. Also scheduling a 30m sync w/ Priya + Lena tomorrow 9:30am PT to coordinate rollout and load test.
Priya (Customer): For reproducibility: we'll run k6 script that opens 120 concurrent tabs (simulates users) hitting the init endpoint. Will paste results.
Lena (SDK Eng): If you can't change SDK immediately, we can ship a patched devkit that includes singleflight + token lease behavior and a conservative retry/backoff (exponential with jitter, cap attempts at 3). ETA for canary build ~18h.
Raj (SRE): If you provide the k6 script we'll run it with the soft-queue enabled and monitor 429 rate vs success-queued responses. Also request logs showing X-Client-Instance header so we can detect multi-tab fanout.
deploy-bot: canary release v1.3.1-edgefix deployed to 5% of edge fleet. Watch 429 and latency for 45m.
Priya (Customer): Canary looks promising — 429s down ~60% on the canary cohort. We'll proceed with staged rollout.
Anya (CS): Great. Once rollout finishes we'll capture remediation steps into the onboarding checklist (token leases, singleflight example, k6 repro), and add a note in the account health doc marking this as a near-term renewal risk that is now mitigated.
Priya (Customer): Thanks all — I'll upload the k6 output and mark the issue resolved after full prod verification.
